    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0761" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/132</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lindsay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-26">26 September, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 365</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>; With reference to my note No. 350 of the
                    18th instant<anchor n="72" xml:id="d510-f1"/> and previous correspondence
                    regarding the proposed preliminary conference of the Governments of the
                    countries in which narcotic drugs are manufactured, I have the honour to inform
                    you that I have now received <pb facs="0762" n="648" xml:id="pg648"/> the reply
                    of His Majesty’s Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs to the points
                    raised in your note of the 12th instant.</p>
                <p>Mr. Henderson<anchor n="73" xml:id="d510-f2"/> states that the matters to be
                    discussed at the preliminary conference are indicated in paragraph 8 of appendix
                    5 of the Opium Advisory Committee’s Report on the work of its thirteenth
                        session,<anchor n="74" xml:id="d510-f3"/> and that it is not proposed to
                    bring up any other subjects. Mr. Henderson adds that it is understood that Mr.
                    Caldwell has already received direct from the League of Nations the documents
                    which have hitherto been issued for the use of the preliminary conference, that
                    further documents are in course of preparation and that it is presumed that Mr.
                    Caldwell will receive them in due course.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Lindsay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
